        "raw": "<p>Literally this time. &nbsp;I just reported the bug, but it was too fun to leave at that.</p><p>Playing Kaargra Warfang on Challenge in Atlantis. &nbsp;Kaargra was down to 12 HP, I had the 20 points, she had 12 I think. &nbsp;Then Pillars of Hercules came out. &nbsp;Bad but not too bad, ended her turn with 15 points. &nbsp;Since most of her cards are gladiators, I&#39;m not worried, I should win before she gets another turn.</p><p>Problem: Pillars causes her to play Get Back In There on my turn. &nbsp;She gets, you guessed it, 5 gladiators. &nbsp;Of course, Challenge mode tries to put Title cards under each of them as they come out. &nbsp;However, the title deck was empty. &nbsp;Here&#39;s where the glitch comes in: instead of Title cards being revealed, normal cards from Kaargra&#39;s villain deck are revealed. &nbsp;Since they&#39;re not titles, the message was &quot;Ashclaw Revelos earned the title !&quot; for instance. &nbsp;And looking at them, they had titles under them with no text.</p><p>Unfortunately, the game still awarded them the 5 points for earning 5 titles and I &quot;lost.&quot;</p><p><strong>Edit:</strong> I only just realized that only two gladiators should have been brought out. &nbsp;Which means that I misunderstood what actually happened here. &nbsp;A whole bunch of gladiators did come out, but I think they were actually being&nbsp;<em>played</em>. &nbsp;I have only a partial log (thanks, Android), but it seems that Bloodsworn Judgment was put under&nbsp;Ashclaw R&#39;velos, and then I think another Get Back In There was put under&nbsp;S&#39;sdari the Bloody, which caused more gladiators to be put into play, which caused more cards to be put under them, which effectively played them. &nbsp;I know I saw a Fickle Fans go by at once point. &nbsp;Ugh, I wish I had the full log, it must have been quite the mess.</p>",
